hifiberry-jellyfin (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial package: jellyfin-mpv-shim as a Jellyfin cast target.
    - jellyfin-mpv-shim 3.3.0 and its pure-Python dependencies, pinned by
      hash, in /usr/lib/hifiberry-jellyfin/venv; nothing is downloaded on
      the device
    - start-jellyfin prepares the shim's configuration on every start: the
      mpv template for the hardware (Wayland under kiosk mode, KMS on a
      connected HDMI display, audio only otherwise), hardware decoding for
      the Pi 4 and Pi 5, a headless conf.json named after the device, the
      remote bitrate cap from player.jellyfin.unlimited_remote, and the
      artwork cache audiocontrol reads
    - jellyfin.service, a systemd --user unit, disabled by default
    - jellyfin-setup, enabled by default: signs the device in with Quick
      Connect for the WebUI, finds Jellyfin servers on the LAN for the
      server setting, and signs out again
    - Player descriptor with the server drop-down, a server address field
      and "Full quality over VPN"; audiocontrol, config-server, nginx and
      auth drop-ins for the player and its sign-in API
    - MPRIS on the system bus for audiocontrol, with a D-Bus policy for the
      player user generated on install; the player user joins the render
      group, with a reboot requested only when it had to be added
    - Hardware volume: the Jellyfin volume slider drives the sound card's
      volume control reported by config-server, and follows changes made
      elsewhere; boards without one keep mpv's software volume

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
